# SonarQube Community Build Installation on Rocky Linux 9

## Class Project Guide

This guide explains how to install the open-source **SonarQube Community Build** on a Rocky Linux 9 virtual machine using Docker Compose and PostgreSQL.

---

## 1. Project Architecture

The installation will use:

- Rocky Linux 9
- Docker Engine
- Docker Compose
- SonarQube Community Build
- PostgreSQL
- TCP port `9000`

### Architecture Flow

```text
Student Browser
      |
      | HTTP port 9000
      v
SonarQube Container
      |
      | PostgreSQL port 5432
      v
PostgreSQL Container
```

---

## 2. Recommended VM Resources

A VM with `1 vCPU`, `4 GB RAM`, and `15 GB disk` is too small for a reliable SonarQube installation.

Use the following resources:

| Resource | Minimum | Recommended |
|---|---:|---:|
| vCPU | 2 | 2–4 |
| RAM | 4 GB | 8 GB |
| Disk | 30 GB | 40–50 GB |
| Operating System | Rocky Linux 9 | Rocky Linux 9 |

SonarQube uses Elasticsearch internally, so sufficient memory and disk space are important.

### Verify the VM Resources

```bash
lscpu | grep '^CPU(s)'
free -h
lsblk
df -h /
```

> Increasing the virtual disk in Xen Orchestra does not automatically expand the Linux partition, logical volume, or filesystem.

---

## 3. Update Rocky Linux

Run the following commands as `root`:

```bash
dnf update -y
dnf install -y dnf-plugins-core curl openssl firewalld
```

Set the hostname:

```bash
hostnamectl set-hostname sonarqube
```

Enable and start the firewall:

```bash
systemctl enable --now firewalld
```

Verify:

```bash
hostnamectl
systemctl status firewalld --no-pager
```

---

## 4. Install Docker Engine

Add the Docker repository:

```bash
dnf config-manager --add-repo \
https://download.docker.com/linux/rhel/docker-ce.repo
```

Install Docker Engine and Docker Compose:

```bash
dnf install -y \
docker-ce \
docker-ce-cli \
containerd.io \
docker-buildx-plugin \
docker-compose-plugin
```

Enable and start Docker:

```bash
systemctl enable --now docker
```

Verify the installation:

```bash
docker --version
docker compose version
systemctl status docker --no-pager
```

Test Docker:

```bash
docker run --rm hello-world
```

---

## 5. Configure Linux Kernel Requirements

SonarQube uses Elasticsearch and requires higher Linux kernel limits.

Create the configuration file:

```bash
cat > /etc/sysctl.d/99-sonarqube.conf <<'EOF'
vm.max_map_count=524288
fs.file-max=131072
EOF
```

Apply the settings:

```bash
sysctl --system
```

Verify:

```bash
sysctl vm.max_map_count
sysctl fs.file-max
```

Expected values:

```text
vm.max_map_count = 524288
fs.file-max = 131072
```

Check whether seccomp support is enabled:

```bash
grep SECCOMP /boot/config-$(uname -r)
```

Expected output should include values similar to:

```text
CONFIG_HAVE_ARCH_SECCOMP_FILTER=y
CONFIG_SECCOMP_FILTER=y
CONFIG_SECCOMP=y
```

---

## 6. Create the SonarQube Project Directory

```bash
mkdir -p /opt/sonarqube
cd /opt/sonarqube
```

Generate a strong PostgreSQL password:

```bash
DB_PASSWORD=$(openssl rand -hex 24)
```

Create the environment file:

```bash
cat > .env <<EOF
POSTGRES_DB=sonarqube
POSTGRES_USER=sonarqube
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=${DB_PASSWORD}
EOF
```

Protect the file:

```bash
chmod 600 .env
```

Display and securely record the database password:

```bash
cat .env
```

> Do not upload the `.env` file to a public GitHub repository because it contains the database password.

---

## 7. Create the Docker Compose File

Create the Compose file:

```bash
vi /opt/sonarqube/compose.yml
```

Add the following configuration:

```yaml
services:
  db:
    image: postgres:17
    container_name: sonarqube-db
    restart: unless-stopped

    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: ${POSTGRES_DB}
      POSTGRES_USER: ${POSTGRES_USER}
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}

    volumes:
      - postgresql_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data

    healthcheck:
      test:
        - CMD-SHELL
        - pg_isready -U ${POSTGRES_USER} -d ${POSTGRES_DB}
      interval: 10s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 15

    networks:
      - sonarqube-network

  sonarqube:
    image: sonarqube:community
    container_name: sonarqube
    restart: unless-stopped
    stop_grace_period: 1h

    depends_on:
      db:
        condition: service_healthy

    environment:
      SONAR_JDBC_URL: jdbc:postgresql://db:5432/${POSTGRES_DB}
      SONAR_JDBC_USERNAME: ${POSTGRES_USER}
      SONAR_JDBC_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}

    ports:
      - "9000:9000"

    volumes:
      - sonarqube_data:/opt/sonarqube/data
      - sonarqube_extensions:/opt/sonarqube/extensions
      - sonarqube_logs:/opt/sonarqube/logs

    ulimits:
      nofile:
        soft: 131072
        hard: 131072
      nproc: 8192

    networks:
      - sonarqube-network

networks:
  sonarqube-network:
    name: sonarqube-network

volumes:
  postgresql_data:
  sonarqube_data:
  sonarqube_extensions:
  sonarqube_logs:
```

### Explanation of the Persistent Volumes

| Volume | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `postgresql_data` | Stores the PostgreSQL database |
| `sonarqube_data` | Stores SonarQube indexes and data |
| `sonarqube_extensions` | Stores plugins and extensions |
| `sonarqube_logs` | Stores SonarQube log files |

