## 14. Useful Management Commands

### Start SonarQube

```bash
cd /opt/sonarqube
docker compose start
```

### Stop SonarQube

```bash
cd /opt/sonarqube
docker compose stop
```

### Restart SonarQube

```bash
cd /opt/sonarqube
docker compose restart
```

### View All Logs

```bash
cd /opt/sonarqube
docker compose logs -f
```

### View SonarQube Logs

```bash
docker compose logs -f sonarqube
```

### View PostgreSQL Logs

```bash
docker compose logs -f db
```

### Stop and Remove the Containers

```bash
docker compose down
```

This command removes the containers and network but keeps the persistent volumes.

### Dangerous Command

```bash
docker compose down -v
```

> Warning: The `-v` option deletes the PostgreSQL database and SonarQube persistent data volumes.

