## 16. Common Problems and Troubleshooting

### Problem 1: SonarQube Keeps Restarting

Check the container status:

```bash
docker compose ps
```

Check the logs:

```bash
docker compose logs --tail=200 sonarqube
```

Verify the kernel settings:

```bash
sysctl vm.max_map_count
sysctl fs.file-max
```

Required values:

```text
vm.max_map_count = 524288
fs.file-max = 131072
```

---

### Problem 2: Container Is Killed Because of Low Memory

Check memory:

```bash
free -h
docker stats --no-stream
```

Check for Out-of-Memory events:

```bash
dmesg -T | grep -iE 'out of memory|oom|killed process'
```

Increase the VM to at least `8 GB RAM` if SonarQube and PostgreSQL are running on the same VM.

---

### Problem 3: PostgreSQL Connection Failure

Check PostgreSQL logs:

```bash
docker compose logs --tail=200 db
```

Test PostgreSQL readiness:

```bash
docker compose exec db \
pg_isready -U sonarqube -d sonarqube
```

Verify the values in the `.env` file:

```bash
cat /opt/sonarqube/.env
```

---

### Problem 4: SonarQube Web Page Does Not Open

Test SonarQube locally:

```bash
curl -I http://127.0.0.1:9000
```

Check whether port `9000` is listening:

```bash
ss -lntp | grep 9000
```

Check the firewall:

```bash
firewall-cmd --list-ports
```

Check the containers:

```bash
docker compose ps
```

---

### Problem 5: Disk Space Is Full

Check disk usage:

```bash
df -h
docker system df
```

Check Docker storage usage:

```bash
du -sh /var/lib/docker/*
```

Do not use the following command without understanding what it may delete:

```bash
docker volume prune
```

It could remove volumes that contain required application data.

---

## 17. Optional: Give SonarQube a Static IP Address

Example NetworkManager configuration:

```bash
nmcli connection show
```

Replace `enX0` with the actual connection name:

```bash
nmcli connection modify enX0 \
  ipv4.method manual \
  ipv4.addresses 192.168.1.220/24 \
  ipv4.gateway 192.168.1.1 \
  ipv4.dns "192.168.1.1 8.8.8.8"
```

Apply the configuration:

```bash
nmcli connection down enX0
nmcli connection up enX0
```

Verify:

```bash
ip -4 address show enX0
ip route
```

> An SSH session may disconnect when the network connection is restarted.

